        "Unresolved": [
          "UNRESOLVED (p.35 / p.36 (S0-34 / S0-35 location sketches)): -L- state plane coordinates of the PIs / PCs - the structure plans print no N / E for the -L- PI / PC / PT; only the GPS monument B2500-2 (N 751499.622, E 3031964.117 US ft, -L- STA 26\u002B47.55, 23.82\u0027 RT) is given. The alignment is placed by that monument (curve 1 PI 27\u002B27.13 R 2,347 LT, printed tangent bearings, p.21-34 curve data; check: long chord 794.52 ft vs 794\u0027-6 1/4\u0022 printed); the direction of increasing stations (towards N 0 44\u0027 E) rests on the printed bearings \u002B the location sketch. PC / PT N / E in docs/plan-data/bonner-b2500/L-coordinates.csv.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p4): cross slope transition 70\u002B28.93 - 70\u002B82.93 (4.5% to 2.5%) - S0-03 prints \u0027varies\u0027 and refers to the roadway plans, which are not in this set. Linear in station between the two printed slopes.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.263, 268): relation of the span lengths (horizontal, along -L-) to the segment lengths (chords along the girder CL) - the plans state both conventions and give no conversion or casting geometry. Joints are placed at their -L- stations; each segment is the straight 3D chord between its joint WPs; the chord offset from -L- and the chord-minus-station length are reported by the generator.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.271): end segment start 10\u0022 from the bent 18 / 29 control line - derived (9\u0027-6\u0022 to the closure face minus 8\u0027-8\u0022), not printed. Used as derived.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.267): casting curve / camber / segment survey geometry - not in the plans (geometry control gives final WP positions only). Box modeled at the final profile, no camber.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.305): T6 only at bents 22-25 and T14 only at bents 19 and 28 - printed so in the schedule without explanation (T6 drawn dashed with T5). Modeled as printed.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.278): number of bent segments with transverse tendons F1 \u0026 F2 - the S3-30 table lists 18 (and 9 for the longitudinal bars) while 10 cantilever bents have 20 split halves. Each of the 20 bent halves gets F1 \u0026 F2 (difference reported by the check).",
          "[details] UNRESOLVED (p.299-300): temporary PT bars between the bent segment and U1, and the permanent 1 3/4\u0022 bent PT bars with their pockets - their anchor plates sit in the bent segment at positions that are drawn only (\u00273\u0027-0\u0022 MIN.\u0027), and the pocket outline of the permanent bars (Section C-C) is not dimensioned. Not built.",
          "[details] UNRESOLVED (p.285-296): anchor block pattern at bents 21, 23, 25 and 27 - the layout sheets show bents 19, 20, 22, 24, 26 and 28 only (the key elevations that name the other bents were not read). The identical pattern of every sheet is used (B_k in segment k\u002B4, end spans k\u002B6; C1 / C2 in 10 / 11).",
          "[details] UNRESOLVED (p.271, 277): end segment diaphragm opening, bearing pintle blockouts - the end segment is modeled as a solid envelope (its opening width 10\u0027-2\u0022 is scaled) and the pintles go through the bent soffit with the bearing details. Not built. (Vent holes, survey blockouts, deck drains, access doors, vermin screens, solar platforms and box lighting are built by misc-bonner-unit5.csx.)",
          "[details] UNRESOLVED (p.392, 263-266): navigational lights and their conduit runs - the lights, junction boxes and cable are by others and located only relative to the navigation channel, whose CL station is not given; only the cast-in conduit sleeves are dimensioned. Not built (sleeves only, in misc-bonner-unit5.csx).",
          "[details] UNRESOLVED (p.283): bottom slab alignment keys at the bent control line and the R = 1\u0022 key transitions - the bent control line section shows the bottom slab keys without dimensions (solid diaphragm zone) and the transitions are drawn as 1\u0022 radii. Bottom slab keys at the bent control line not built; key flanks straight (trapezoid).",
          "[rebar] UNRESOLVED (p.270): #4A16 bottom slab duct bars and the D-4 anchorage wire - \u00272-#4A16 at every tendon in the bottom slab crossing a joint\u0027 and the D-4 wire have no bend dimensions and are not in the bill; the transverse PT sheet for the wire is not tabulated. Not scheduled or placed.",
          "[rebar] UNRESOLVED (p.281): closure joint A1-A4, A8, A9, A13-A15, S1 and web B1 bars - the closure sheet labels these marks without counts (and #4A13 OR #4A14 without the split). Not scheduled or placed.",
          "[rebar] UNRESOLVED (p.279-280): bent segment marks N2, N8, N10, N11, N13-N37, N39-N44 and S1 / A9 at the bent - they are drawn with partial counts (\u0027VARIES\u0027, \u0027(\u002B/-)\u0027) and shapes only, with no bill of materials. Not scheduled or placed.",
          "[rebar] UNRESOLVED (p.273-276): end segment marks E1-E8, E16-E44, E46-E48, S1 / S2 / A9 - they are drawn with counts in elevation / section views of the anchor zone but without a bill of materials or bend dimensions, and the end segment interior (diaphragm, blockout) is not modeled. Not scheduled or placed.",
          "[rebar] UNRESOLVED (p.297-302, 321): anchor block J / T, erection block P, deviation block D and opening H bars - the block sheets give counts and spacings with shapes drawn only and no bill of materials; the blocks themselves carry dimension-only flags. Not scheduled or placed (block solids by details-bonner-unit5.csx)."
        ],
        "Reported": [
          "Alignment: curve 2 R x delta - printed L = \u002B0.003 ft; ahead tangent from R / L vs printed N 45 04\u002744.5\u0022 W: -0.2\u0022",
